                                        <div class="tab-pane fade active show" id="pills-1" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="Introduction"><p align="justify">The School of Social Sciences (SOSS) at IGNOU is among the largest schools of the university, offering a broad spectrum of programmes across eight key disciplines: Anthropology, Economics, History, Library and Information Science, Sociology, Political Science, Psychology, and Public Administration. In addition to the eight disciplines, Centre for Gandhian Studies is also attached with the School of Social Sciences. The School is particularly noted for its interdisciplinary courses that connect core subjects with related fields. Unique programmes such as the MA in Gandhi and Peace Studies, Post Graduate Diploma in Disaster Risk Reduction and Management, and Post Graduate Diploma in Rehabilitation Psychology exemplify SOSS’s dedication to addressing current socio-economic and political challenges.<br/>
<br/>
The School continually updates its curriculum in tune with national educational policies and is highly responsive to contemporary societal changes. It uses modern ICT tools for open and distance learning, enhancing accessibility for learners across the country. The SOSS has a strong presence on digital platforms, delivering teaching-learning through the Gyan Darshan Channel, Gyan Vani FM Radio platform as well as via multiple online platforms such as YouTube, Facebook Live, Instagram, dedicated online portals, and Swayam/Swayam Prabha. The adoption of multiple digital platforms facilitates accessible and effective distance learning, allowing a large number of students to participate and benefit from the programmes.<br/>
<br/>
One of the key features of the School of Social Sciences (SOSS) is its 'Discussion Forum,' which serves as a platform to engage in multidisciplinary discussions on issues related to social change and development. This Forum places a strong emphasis on fostering critical thinking among participants, encouraging thoughtful debate and the exchange of ideas on contemporary social topics.<br/>
<br/>
A majority of IGNOU’s students are enrolled in SOSS programme, which also indicates the popularity of the programmes offered by the school of social sciences. The school has a robust academic team with over 40 faculty members specializing in different disciplines, further supporting its extensive research and teaching output. Several retired professors from the School of Social Sciences have advanced to leadership roles as Vice Chancellor, PVC, Registrar at various universities across India. At present, two professors from SOSS continue to uphold this tradition by serving as vice chancellors, reflecting the school’s strong legacy of academic leadership and governance.<br/>
<br/>
In summary, School of Social Sciences stands out for its inclusive, up-to-date, and multidisciplinary educational offerings, supporting learners from diverse backgrounds through flexible, technology-enabled, and practice-oriented programmes.<br/>
<br/>

The School currently offers a range of programmes at different levels, including PhD, Master’s Degree, Bachelor’s Degree, Post Graduate Diplomas, and Certificate Programmes.<br/>
<br/>
