                                        <div class="tab-pane fade" id="pills-4" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="Achievements"  ><p align="justify"><ul>
<li>The School of Social Sciences stands as the oldest and largest school in the university, distinguished by its highest student enrolment.</li>
<li>It offers the widest range of academic programmes available at the university.</li>
<li>Students and alumni from this school have attained significant accomplishments across various sectors worldwide.</li>
<li>The faculty comprises highly qualified and experienced professionals who have held roles in diverse institutions and organizations.</li>
<li>Several professors from the School of Social Sciences have advanced to leadership roles as Vice Chancellor, PVC, Registrar at various universities across India. At present, two professors from SOSS continue to uphold this tradition by serving as vice chancellors, reflecting the school’s strong legacy of academic leadership and governance.</li></ul></p></div>
                                    </div>
                                    <div>
                                        

                                        <div class="tab-pane fade" id="pills-5" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="Director&#39;sMessage"  ><p>School of Social Sciences provides prospective learners with a wide variety of programmes in the subject areas that are popular as well as socially relevant. The School offers various programmes pertaining to eight disciplines (Anthropology, Economics, History, Library and Information Science, Political Science, Psychology and Sociology) that are housed in the School. The programmes are offered at undergraduate, masters and doctoral levels. Besides the school also offered post graduate diploma and diploma and certificate programmes. Some of the programmes offered by the School, like MA (Psychology) and Masters in Library and Information Science also have internship component that helps learners in gaining hands on experience. Further, many programmes also have components like practicum, field work, project, that help learner develop an overall understanding of the subject area.</p></div>
